  "notes": "Source: The University of Texas at Austin School of Nursing, 'BACHELOR OF SCIENCE DEGREE IN NURSING - Degree Plan Worksheet, 2024-2026 Catalog Requirements' (updated 04/15/24), https://nursing.utexas.edu/sites/default/files/documents/bsn_degree_plan_2024_2026_1_0.pdf. Cross-checked against catalog.utexas.edu: the live BSN catalog page (2026-2028 Undergraduate Catalog) states the program is '125 to 126 semester hours of coursework' (http://catalog.utexas.edu/undergraduate/nursing/degrees-and-programs/bs-nursing/), and current General Information catalog course descriptions confirm N 244 (2 hrs, 'Perinatal Nursing Care'), N 344P (3 hrs, 'Perinatal Nursing Care Practicum'), N 255C/255D (2 hrs each), N 355P (3 hrs), N 354 (3 hrs), and INB 446L (4 hrs, 'Human Microscopic and Gross Anatomy'). Transcription method: read the worksheet's term-by-term tables directly from the official PDF text; worksheet term labels (Freshman/Sophomore/Junior/Senior 1st & 2nd Semester, Summer 1st Year) mapped to Fall/Spring/Summer Year N. Caveats: (1) Catalog year is 2024-2026 (the worksheet's stated catalog); the 2026-2028 catalog keeps the same 125-126 hour BSN program per the live catalog page, but the School of Nursing has not published a newer worksheet. (2) Degree total is 125-126: this plan sums to 126 using the worksheet's listed HDF 313 + HDF 113L (4 hrs) option for the child-development slot; the catalog also allows PSY 304 (3 hrs), which would make the total 125. (3) PHM 338 Pharmacology (3 hrs) is listed by the worksheet as 'Summer: PHM338' - taught in summer, fall, and spring; must be taken after N 320 and before the Senior I semester; counted here in Spring Year 3 to match the worksheet's stated 15-hour Junior 2nd Semester total. (4) N 244/N 344P titles use the current catalog's official course titles ('Perinatal Nursing Care' / 'Perinatal Nursing Care Practicum'); the worksheet labels them 'Nursing Care of Childbearing Families'. (5) Prereq arrays left empty per hub convention - the worksheet does not publish per-course prerequisites; the catalog states nursing courses must be taken in a specific sequence.",
